= INTRODUCTION
== Background
Parking is an essential part of modern transportation infrastructure, allowing vehicles to be stored safely when not in use. As vehicle ownership and urban mobility continue to increase, the demand for efficient parking facilities has grown across cities, institutions, and commercial areas. Unlike roadways, which support vehicle movement, parking spaces are designed for organized vehicle storage over short or extended periods. Effective parking management helps reduce congestion, improves safety, and enhances the overall efficiency and convenience of urban environments. 

Number plates @PLATE play a vital role in vehicle identification and traffic management, providing a unique identity for vehicles in applications such as parking management, toll collection, traffic surveillance, and law enforcement. With advancements in computer vision and artificial intelligence, ANPR @ANPR has emerged as a reliable method for detecting and recognizing license plates from images and video streams. However, In Nepal, parking systems remain largely manual, relying on handwritten tickets and approximate billing, which leads to inefficiency, human error, lack of transparency, and congestion during peak hours. To address these challenges, this project proposes an Real-Time Smart Parking Billing System Using YOLO and OCR based on ANPR  that automates vehicle entry, exit, and billing by integrating YOLO @YOLO for real-time vehicle and license plate detection with OCR for character recognition, ensuring accurate identification and fair, time-based billing.
