== Gap Identification
In Nepal, parking management is still mostly manual, relying on handwritten tickets and rough, fixed billing methods. This approach is slow, error-prone, and offers little transparency for users or operators. As vehicle numbers continue to rise in urban areas, the absence of automated parking systems has become increasingly noticeable. In particular, ANPR based solutions tailored to Nepal’s local infrastructure and license plate formats are rarely adopted. This gap between existing practices and modern smart parking technologies clearly points to the need for an automated, vision-based parking billing system suited to the Nepali context.
== Motivation
The increasing number of vehicles in urban areas of Nepal has intensified challenges related to parking congestion, inefficient billing, and poor space management. Manual parking systems are time-consuming, prone to error, and lack transparency, leading to inconvenience for both users and operators. Motivated by the need for an efficient, low-cost, and scalable solution, this project aims to leverage computer vision and artificial intelligence to automate parking management. By using ANPR based vehicle identification with YOLO and OCR, the proposed system seeks to reduce human intervention, improve billing accuracy, and support smarter urban parking infrastructure in the Nepali context.

== Objectives

The primary objectives of this project are:

- Develop an ANPR system that accurately detects vehicles and recognizes license plates.
- Generate parking bills automatically with minimal error and improved reliability.
- Implement a CNN-based OCR model to accurately extract alphanumeric characters from vehicle number plates.
